==Strategy==
A key progression point thanks to dropping an [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|incredible unit]], I'll Be Bug is a gruelling test of timing.

This stage revolves around the combination of Professor A., who has an immense magnification of 200% here, and Queen Mother V. As the Professor A. is highly buffed, [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] is a mandatory pick for the stage, being able to tank the Professor A. and Weaken him, helping out your other units. However, this is where Her Majesty steps in. She is a potent supporting enemy, having a far-reaching Long Distance attack that applies her debilitating Curse effect, which is guaranteed and lasts for almost 2 MINUTES. This is what turns the stage into a timing test; should you poorly time an anti-Red cat, they would get hit by the Curse and become a waste of cash. This is especially true for Roe Cat, whose consistent timing is key to beating the stage.

Your goal is to consistently time Roe Cats into Queen Mother V.'s blindspot, then timing more units to exploit Roe's Weaken and whittle down the Professor A. and maybe even Queen Mother V, while your units also have to fend off Relic Doges and One Horns. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] are adept at this. Don't take too long though, as in little under two and a half minutes, a second Professor A. spawns. If the first Professor A. hasn't fallen or at the very least close to dying, you'll lose on the spot. However, you can play aggressively and rush down the first Professor A., after which you'll send Her Majesty to the guillotine before the second Professor A. even spawns.

An approach you can take is letting the first Ginger Snache attack your base, but in exchange luring the Professor A. and Queen Mother V, making timing much easier. A specific version of this is with upgraded base health. This allows you to spawn Roe Cat right after the Ginger Snache attacks your base, gambiting almost all of your base health for a stack of two Roe Cats and luring Queen Mother V close to your base, allowing you to commit a quick regicide.

Finally, due to the combination of Professor A.'s chance to Slow your cats and your reliance on Roe Cat's Weaken proc, there is a considerable RNG factor involved in this stage, so expect to take a number of attempts to clear this stage.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: Roe Cat is the basis for most of your strategies, acting as a tanker and weakener for Professor A, at a minimum of Level 40 for peak performance to comfortably tank, ideally with some investment into Cost Down and Slow Resist Talents, though Slow Resist is optional. You will need to time each one to get into Queen Mother V's blindspot, and you'll have to hope that they don't get cursed by Relic Doge.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: A level 40 Courier Cat has enough health to get one attack off on a weakened Professor A., dealing huge damage and speeding up the battle before the second one arrives, and is also fast enough for easy timing. If you happen to have Courier at level 48 or higher, they can tank a hit from an unweakened Professor A without getting knocked back with the help of two small defense up cat combos, making the stage significantly easier.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Cutter Cat]]: Essentially Courier Cat, but with higher speed, and even higher damage, dealing over '''80k damage''' at level 30 to Professor A, helping by a large margin.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: While not exactly the best attacker against Professor A., It can be helpful for taking out a Relic Doge before it curses your Roe Cats. With investment into Attack and Defense Buff Talents, it could get an attack off, dealing a huge chunk of health.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Most useful for chip damage and sniping a Ginger Snache for extra money,
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]: Manic Island will be your main source of damage for Professor A for most of the fight, making it essential to time it so it doesn't get cursed. The more levels on it, the better.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Paired with the Thunderbolt Cannon, Awakened Bahamut Cat can deal enormous damage to Professor A, or even defeat it outright depending on the time you send him out. He can also be sent out if Queen Mother V is hitting the base in a last ditch effort to knock her back.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
:''Most Ubers for this stage don't have as much as an impact as other Advents. The Ubers listed will be mainly for speeding up the process, rather than being the one to win you the level.''

*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]]: Bane of red enemies, being able to quickly squash the One Horns and Professor As. Just make sure to protect her from the Relic Doges and get her inside the boss' blindspot. You must time her very well and guard her from the ginger snaches- a knockback could mean instant loss.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Single-target DPS unit that basically acts as a better Can Can and is insidiously effective. He works very well with his Strengthen/Cost Down Talents to wipe out the One Horns as well as the Relic Doges, while being replaceable easily if lost. His weakness to Professor A. is at worst trivial given his low range and how most strategies account for them already, making him an excellent choice.
*[[Kuu (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kuu γ]]: Pai-Pai lite. Tanks red units and dishes out considerable damage back to them as [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x9E3XxqsF90 demonstrated by Lucas IV]. She can even have Curse Immunity with Talents, although the effects of doing so is negligible.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]]: Saki, being a fast, long-ranged sniper (stands at 600), can absolutely eradicate Red threats from existence, and her short cooldown allows her to be stacked. However, she is very expensive, can be easily invalidated by curse, has a tiny inner range (500 range blindspot), and as with all target only units, she won't be able to help out on the other threats.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Though vulnerable to Curse, Phonoa's very high speed (30), far-reaching LD multi-hits and huge standing range (600 vs 501) means it can utterly reduce every enemy in the stage to rubble. It still requires a fair bit of support to hold its own within the blindspot, but it usually isn't much of an issue.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]: As long as Cat Machine is not cursed, Cat Machine will whittle down Queen Mother V's and Professor A's health. A level 40 Cat Machine can survive long enough for another Cat Machine, allowing for stacking. Speed up talents and combos are recommended.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: Essentially a much stronger Roe, Convoys can easily infiltrate Queen Mother V's blind spot and prevent Professor A. from attacking your other units by constantly knocking him back, allowing your other units free rein to attack the vulnerable Mother V with barely any resistance. Make sure it doesn't get cursed, though.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)| Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Curse immune, decent speed (16), and freeze & strong against relic and red enemies make her absolutely busted in this stage. Her strong against ability especially means she has incredible bulk and exceeds Dasli levels of DPS at the same level.
*Talented [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]]: With the Target Relic and Curse Immune talents unlocked, Ruri completely breaks this stage by solo tanking all enemies in the stage (red and relic), while also applying weaken. With high enough levels, Ruri can solo the level with no help.
*[[Ken (Uber Rare Cat)|Crimson King of Battle Ken]]: If you happen to own this unit, it will be a massive help for this stage, as it is fast enough to easily infiltrate Queen Mother V's blindspot, and is also immune to Professor A.'s slow and can weaken and is strong against almost every threat in this stage.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: Fast enough to infiltrate Queen Mother V's blind spot and deal insane damage to everything in the stage. Additionally, immune to curse. Just watch out for his health, as Prof. A outranges unless he has a stepping stone.
*[[Victorious Skanda (Uber Rare Cat)|Victorious Skanda]]: This unit acts like a second Thunderbolt Cannon that works very well alongside [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], plus Skanda can weaken red enemies and has a level 2 wave attack as a bonus. With proper timing, his conjure can freeze the Professor A. while Bahamut deals hundreds of thousands of damage, crippling the anteater.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]]: While still vulnerable to the Red peons in this stage, his Conjure can help relief the pressure of this stage and push the enemies back to the base. Both his forms work, however, his Evolved Form is preferred for extra bulk to make it to the frontlines.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]]: Like is counterpart, his Conjure is very valuable in this stage, sacrificing cost and Knockback for quick, high damage burst with his conjurer. His Extra Money ability also helps when sniping peons with his Wave Attack, letting you burst Professor A. down and even filling your wallet if he manages to kill One Horn with it. While he can only usually get one or two hits in himself, his damage is not bad when Strengthened at 50% on his second repositon.
*[[King of Extinction Phono]]: Can completely destroy this stage. If you time him correctly, he can slide into Queen Mother V’s blindspot and destroy everything, since he outranges Professor A. Just make sure to have something to guard his blindspot, such as Roe Cat, Courier, or Manic Island.

